          "case_name": "In re Adoption of Kate S.",
          "citation": "315 Neb. 795 (2024)",
          "court": "Nebraska Supreme Court",
          "year": 2024,
          "date_decided": "2024-01-26",
          "holding": "The court held that petitioners seeking to dispense with a parent's adoption consent on abandonment grounds must prove willful abandonment by clear and convincing evidence, and affirmed the county court's finding that the father had not abandoned the child.",
          "relevance": "The adoption petition was denied for failure of proof, and that denial was affirmed.",
          "quote": "The conduct constituting abandonment must appear by clear and convincing evidence to be willful, intentional, or voluntary, without just cause or excuse.",
